---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import MastheadInfoStrip from '../components/MastheadInfoStrip.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { LANGUAGES } from '../lib/news/languages';

// P10.1: every factual claim on this page is traceable to shipped code.
//
// The previous copy described a product that does not exist: "Sarvam AI voice
// synthesis" and a "Bulbul V3" audio card (no such code anywhere in src/),
// ingestion from "official wire streams (PTI, ANI, PIB)" (the real providers
// are NewsData.io, the Guardian and four RSS feeds), and "10 Indian
// languages" (LANGUAGES ships 13). README's own changelog records the
// homepage copy being cleaned of exactly those claims; this page was missed.
//
// The language count is READ FROM THE SOURCE OF TRUTH rather than typed as a
// number, so adding or removing a language cannot leave this page lying again.
export const prerender = true;

const languageCount = LANGUAGES.length;
---

<Layout
  title="About Us & Transparency Disclosure | NewzWale"
  description="What NewzWale actually does, how the fact-checker reaches a verdict, and what it deliberately does not do."
>
  <Navbar />
  <MastheadInfoStrip />

  <main id="main" class="flex-1 py-12 bg-surface-soft">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-10">

      <div>
        <span class="font-mono-caption text-primary-strong text-xs font-semibold">MISSION & TRANSPARENCY</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mt-1">
          Two things, done honestly.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base text-body mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          NewzWale is a live Indian news feed in {languageCount} languages, and a fact-checker that
          tells you when it does not know. It is not a chatbot, it does not rewrite the news, and it
          does not have an opinion. Everything below describes what the software actually does today
          — not what is planned.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-md">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">We link out, we don't rewrite</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Headlines come from NewsData.io, the Guardian, and the public RSS feeds of The Hindu,
            The Indian Express, NDTV and Mint. Every story links to the publisher. Where we show an
            extract, it is the publisher's own summary quoted verbatim and attributed — we do not
            generate summaries and we do not host article text.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-md">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Evidence decides, not the model</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            A claim is checked against published fact-checks (via Google's Fact Check Tools API,
            which indexes IFCN signatories) and live web sources in parallel. A language model reads
            that evidence and proposes a verdict — then a deterministic gate, which consults no
            model, can only downgrade it. <strong class="text-ink">True</strong> and{' '}
            <strong class="text-ink">False</strong> require independent corroboration before they
            may be issued.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-md">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Six verdicts, including "we don't know"</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            True, False, Partly true, Misleading, Needs context, and{' '}
            <strong class="text-ink">Unverified</strong>. That last one is the point: when the
            evidence does not support a call, the answer is that it does not support a call. There
            is no confidence percentage, because a number would imply a precision the method does
            not have.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-md">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Ranked by coverage, not clicks</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            Trending ranks stories by how many independent outlets are covering them, weighted
            toward recency. Not by views, shares or engagement — NewzWale collects none of those, so
            ranking on them would mean inventing a popularity signal we do not have.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="p-6 bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-md">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Your saved articles stay on your device</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
          There are no accounts and no sign-in. Saved articles, your topic choices, and your
          fact-check history are stored in your browser's local storage on the device you used —
          they are never sent to a server. Nothing syncs between devices: saving an article on your
          phone will not make it appear on your laptop, and clearing your browser data clears the
          list. NewzWale can install as an app and its shell works offline, but it will not show you
          a fact-check verdict from a cache — a verdict is only meaningful against the evidence
          fetched for it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Read the method</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          The full account of how a claim moves from input to verdict — the sources consulted, the
          corroboration rule, and what each verdict is allowed to mean — is on the{' '}
          <a
            href="/methodology"
            class="font-semibold text-primary-strong underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink"
            >methodology page</a
          >. If a verdict looks wrong, that page tells you exactly which step to blame.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">What NewzWale does not do</h2>
        <ul class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>No audio or voice synthesis of any kind.</li>
          <li>
            No interface translation. The language selector changes which language the{' '}
            <em>news</em> is fetched in; the buttons and labels stay in English.
          </li>
          <li>No accounts, no profiles, no cross-device sync.</li>
          <li>No hosted article bodies — every story links out to its publisher.</li>
          <li>No direct feed from PTI, ANI or PIB, and no government-release ingestion.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
